{"header":"<h1>Module <code><span>Optimise.Stepper</span></code></h1>","type":"documentation","uses_katex":false,"breadcrumbs":[{"name":"Index","href":"../../../../../../index.html","kind":"leaf-page"},{"name":"owl-base","href":"../../../../../index.html","kind":"page"},{"name":"Owl_neural_graph","href":"../../../../index.html","kind":"module"},{"name":"Make","href":"../../../index.html","kind":"module"},{"name":"Neuron","href":"../../index.html","kind":"argument-1"},{"name":"Optimise","href":"../index.html","kind":"module"},{"name":"Stepper","href":"#","kind":"module"}],"toc":[],"source_anchor":null,"preamble":"<p>Stepper module</p>","content":"<div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec type anchored\" id=\"type-state\"><a href=\"#type-state\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">type</span> state</span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>Optimiser state carried between steps: gradient history, momentum and learning rate caches, and the step counter.</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-init\"><a href=\"#val-init\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> init : \u000A  <span><span class=\"optlabel\">?gs</span>:<span><span><a href=\"../Algodiff/index.html#type-t\">Algodiff.t</a> array</span> array</span> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span>\u000A  <span><a href=\"../Params/index.html#type-typ\">Params.typ</a> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span>\u000A  <span><span><span><a href=\"../Algodiff/index.html#type-t\">Algodiff.t</a> array</span> array</span> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span>\u000A  <a href=\"#type-state\">state</a></span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p><code>init ~gs params ws</code> creates a single-step optimiser for weights <code>ws</code>, e.g. those returned by <code>Graph.mkpri</code>. Only the <code>gradient</code>, <code>learning_rate</code>, <code>momentum</code> and <code>clipping</code> fields of <code>params</code> are used; regularisation should be added to the loss by the caller.</p><p><code>gs</code> seeds the gradient history and is required by the conjugate gradient methods. Newton methods are not supported.</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-step\"><a href=\"#val-step\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> step : \u000A  <span><a href=\"#type-state\">state</a> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span>\u000A  <span><span><span><a href=\"../Algodiff/index.html#type-t\">Algodiff.t</a> array</span> array</span> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span>\u000A  <span><span><span><a href=\"../Algodiff/index.html#type-t\">Algodiff.t</a> array</span> array</span> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span>\u000A  <span><span><a href=\"../Algodiff/index.html#type-t\">Algodiff.t</a> array</span> array</span></span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p><code>step state ws gs</code> takes one optimisation step from weights <code>ws</code> with gradients <code>gs</code> (e.g. as returned by <code>Graph.backward</code>) and returns the new weights. The step uses the same update rule as <code>minimise_network</code>.</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-count\"><a href=\"#val-count\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> count : <span><a href=\"#type-state\">state</a> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> int</span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p><code>count state</code> returns the number of steps taken so far.</p></div></div>"}